  "details": "In the new UI, there are various regions where an image is used as a button to advance a screen, return to a previous screen, or initiate an action. However, in many cases, these buttons only work if the cursor is placed directly on the image. \nThis is a problem for buttons where the selectable area has thin regions, like the back button in the top left of some menus, or buttons indicated primarily by text. It makes these buttons behave in an unreliable manner. \nThe most notable button I've found this on is the aforementioned back button, which seems difficult to click.",
